@capability-staffage-cast
Feature: Casts export fast without changing a picture
  The cast exporter is the expensive step of every clip render. Its work is cut by exact algorithms only: a linear exact distance transform, a window that visits only the cells that can matter,
  a memo of repeated shapes, one shared history for the frames of a clip, and frames that are placed and written one at a time. The pictures stay the same. The vectors live in
  `🧫️fixtures/🚀️export-performance/🔣️.json`.

  THE REFERENCES are scipy (`ndimage.distance_transform_edt`), the pinned widths of the corrected measure (regenerated by the ticket script, checked by shapely), the analytic widths of simple shapes and a
  brute-force distance oracle.

  Scenario: The distance transform equals scipy and brute force
    Given explicit and seeded images, with a reused scratch and with a window of read cells
    When the squared distance of every cell to the nearest source is computed
    Then it equals scipy's transform, equals brute force, and inside a window it is exact wherever the distance is within the cap

  Scenario: The feature width of a shape is unchanged
    Given rectangles, an L, a disk, an annulus, a comb and a shape that fills the raster cap
    When the feature width is measured twice
    Then it equals the pinned value bit for bit, agrees with shapely, lies within a tenth of a millimetre of the analytic width and a shape that differs by one coordinate is measured afresh

  Scenario: A shape that is provably wide enough is not measured to the end
    Given the same shapes and a width they must reach
    When the feature width is asked with that width as lower limit
    Then the answer is the exact width or a bound between the limit and the exact width, and the exact width is still measured afresh afterwards

  Scenario: Frames solved with a shared thermal session equal frames solved alone
    Given a looping walk cycle and a radiator under an environment timeline, solved at times in any order, repeated and far beyond the history window
    When each frame is solved with one shared session and again alone
    Then every thermal field is identical and the shared run asks the asset for fewer evaluations

  Scenario: Exported frames are pinned
    Given the clip, thermal clip, transient and pose casts of the cast-export fixture
    When they are exported
    Then every frame equals its pinned SHA-256 (measured values to four significant digits), identical frames are written once and no helper file is left behind

  Scenario: Cost stays linear
    Given a 2.5 million cell raster and a shape that fills the raster cap
    When they are transformed and measured
    Then the CPU time stays far below the budget that a return to the quadratic work would exceed
